     * Omitted fields stay absent, empty strings stay empty, and null or absent data is a payload mismatch.
     *
     * Documented: Removing the named security key is irreversible; the client provides no recovery or rollback.
     * Removing a key still referenced by registrar DS records can break DNSSEC validation, so coordinate the registrar
     * DS change before removal. The response key_id is documented as a string and is preserved unchanged; the request
     * key_id is an integer identifier.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:DNSSEC/remove_zone_key#GET (wire name remove_zone_key).
     *
     * @param string $domain The security key's domain.
     * @param int $keyId The security key's ID.
     * @return RemoveZoneKeyResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/dns-security/dnssec-remove_zone_key
     */
    public function removeZoneKey(string $domain, int $keyId): array
    {
        /** @var RemoveZoneKeyResult $result Validated against DnssecSpec::REMOVE_ZONE_KEY. */
        $result = ($this->run)(DnssecSpec::REMOVE_ZONE_KEY, ['domain' => $domain, 'keyId' => $keyId]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Update domain to use NSEC3.
     *
     * This function configures the domain to use Next Secure Record 3 (NSEC3) semantics.
     *
     * Documented: Available from cPanel 60; operates on the selected account. Disabling the DNS role disables this
     * operation. The client performs no automatic retry or rollback.
     *
     * Documented: Configures NSEC3 semantics. nsec3_iterations=0 remains zero; nsec3_narrow and nsec3_opt_out use bool
     * inputs encoded as 0/1. Only select opt-out when records for all delegations are required, per the pinned
     * description. cPanel 132 and later accepts nsec3_salt='-' to indicate no salt. The optional enabled map contains
     * per-domain integer 0/1 results separate from envelope status.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:DNSSEC/set_nsec3#GET (wire name set_nsec3).
     *
     * @param string $domain The domain on which to enable NSEC3 semantics.
     * @param int $nsec3Iterations The number of times that the system re-executes the first resource record hash
     *     operation.
     * @param bool $nsec3Narrow Whether NSEC3 will operate in Narrow mode or Inclusive mode.
     * @param bool $nsec3OptOut Whether the system will create records for all delegations.
     * @param string $nsec3Salt The salt value that PowerDNS uses in the hashes.
     * @return SetNsec3Result
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
     * @throws PayloadMismatchException If the API envelope reported success but the payload differs from the contract;
     *     the operation may already have changed state; do not retry automatically.
     * @see https://api.docs.cpanel.net/specifications/cpanel.openapi/dns-security/dnssec-set_nsec3
     */
    public function setNsec3(
        string $domain,
        int $nsec3Iterations,
        bool $nsec3Narrow,
        bool $nsec3OptOut,
        string $nsec3Salt,
    ): array {
        /** @var SetNsec3Result $result Validated against DnssecSpec::SET_NSEC3. */
        $result = ($this->run)(DnssecSpec::SET_NSEC3, [
            'domain' => $domain,
            'nsec3Iterations' => $nsec3Iterations,
            'nsec3Narrow' => $nsec3Narrow,
            'nsec3OptOut' => $nsec3OptOut,
            'nsec3Salt' => $nsec3Salt,
        ]);

        return $result;
    }

    /**
     * Update domain to use NSEC.
     *
     * This function configures the domain to use Next Secure Record (NSEC) semantics instead of Next Secure Record 3
     * (NSEC3) semantics.
     *
     * Documented: Available from cPanel 60; operates on the selected account. Disabling the DNS role disables this
     * operation. The client performs no automatic retry or rollback.
     *
